{
  "_about": "Real v1 storage (pg-assistant-sessions-v1). Shapes from AssistantPanel.turns.ts and what AssistantPanel.tsx wrote: JSON.stringify({ sessions, activeId, mode, modeChosen }) of live state, so undoable and proposal clones reach storage. everyKind is live state, one turn of every v1 kind: you, building (running and awaiting), built (completed, stopped by signal with undone sections, stopped by budget, stopped by the person when the run threw before the engine's own ending), thinking, stopped (with and without a receipt), refused (full), discarded, outline (with and without sections) and plan (applied, unapplied in Ask, unapplied in Plan). revivedByV1 is what v1 itself wrote back after every load (its persist effect saves reviveSessions' output on mount), so it is the commonest shape in real browsers: a building revived as built (stopped: true, no request, rows still running, no engine time), built stripped of request, undoable and undone counters (completed, and stopped by the engine before its own ending), plans stripped of impact, salvaged, run and authority, and the refusals v1 never revived because it wrote them in their final shape: the build path's (failure and request, no receipt), an apply's (failure, no request) and the plan path's (text and request, no failure: v1's Plan-mode catch kept only the thrown error's message, or \"The plan could not be written.\" when there was none, and settled it retryable). Every engine string is one a real engine version wrote: run-build.ts's section reasons, remote-provider.ts's \"The assistant server answered with status N.\" and \"could not be reached\", the kernel door's refusals as validate-plan.ts and salvage-plan.ts phrase them. legacy is data from before receipts, modes and unique ids.",
